## MANUAL — walked per the dispatch, both themes

**Glide checkbox (D6).** Traced with Playwright (`trace1_glide.mjs`):
keyboard-focus the checkbox, press Space → `checked` flips true, no
`/whatif/glide-path` request fires (confirms D6's "reveal only, no submit on
tick"), `#glide-path-fields.hidden` is removed. While unchecked/hidden, the
Start-% field's `offsetParent` is null (genuinely non-interactive/unreachable
by Tab, not merely visually hidden) — hidden fields are not focusable while
hidden, satisfies AC. Tabbing from the checkbox lands on
`glide-start-stock-pct` → `glide-end-stock-pct` → `glide-transition-years` in
order, each with its own `<label for>` ("Start %"/"End %"/"Years") — fields
labelled and reachable in visual order (point 9). Reveal state: no
`aria-expanded`/`aria-controls` on the checkbox — judged against point 9/16's
"or equivalent" wording as an ACCEPTABLE equivalent (native
checkbox checked/unchecked state is itself exposed to the accessibility tree,
and the revealed region is the checkbox's own immediately-following DOM/tab
sibling, not a disconnected or off-screen region needing aria-controls to
locate) — OBSERVATION, not a FAIL; aria-controls would still be a cheap
enhancement.

**Glide error (D6).** `trace2_glide_error.mjs`: ticking + clicking "Apply
Glide Path" with all three fields blank inserts
`<div role="alert">…Start %, End %, and Years are all required…</div>` as the
FIRST CHILD of the glide `<form>` (next to the form — point 5's aria-live
alternative branch, reusing the existing WS4 `renderError`/base.js
`htmx:responseError` mechanism, unchanged by this diff). Announced once:
repeating the identical failing click leaves exactly 1 `[role=alert]` node
(the existing-text short-circuit in base.js). Focus stays on the Apply
button — not moved into the error and not lost to `<body>` (satisfies point
5's aria-live-announces branch; point 5's literal "linked via
aria-describedby" is not implemented here, but that is the same
already-established, unchanged-by-this-diff sitewide `renderError` pattern
every other `/whatif` error uses since WS4 — PRE-EXISTING, OBSERVATION).

**Person Remove / refusal (D7).** `trace3_person_remove.mjs`: Enter on
Christine's Remove button (keyboard-activated) → optimistic DOM removal,
debounced save (500ms) comes back refused →
`<div role="alert">…Remove Christine's healthcare entry first</div>` lands as
the first child of the SETTINGS `<form>` (next to the form), the row is
restored (2 person-rows again, Christine's data intact), and — confirmed —
focus returns to Christine's own Remove button (`focusedIsRemoveButton:
true`), never falling to `<body>`. This exactly matches the dispatch's ask
and PASSES cleanly.

**Person Remove accessible name.** Both the server-rendered row (template
`data-remove-person-row` button) and the JS-generated row
(`addPersonRow()` in whatif-rate-assumptions.js) render the button's only
accessible text as the bare word "Remove" — no name, no `aria-label`.
Confirmed via `git show master:web/templates/components/whatif/rate-assumptions.html`
and `git show master:web/static/js/whatif-rate-assumptions.js` — byte-
identical to master in both places (WS5.1.diff never touches this markup).
PRE-EXISTING — OBSERVATION, but worth flagging loudly: D7 makes Remove a
real, persisting, sometimes-refused action, so two non-primary rows now
produce two keyboard-indistinguishable "Remove" controls in the accessible
name. Recommend `aria-label="Remove {{.Name}}"` server-side and the JS
equivalent as a fast follow.

**Successful (non-refused) removal — focus loss.** `trace8_success_focus.mjs`:
added a valid unlinked person ("Sam"), removed her — save succeeds — and
focus falls to `<body>` and stays there. Checked master's prior
`removePersonRow` (`git show master:web/static/js/whatif-rate-assumptions.js`):
it was a synchronous `row.remove()` with the same "focused control vanishes,
nothing restores focus" root cause, so this exact failure mode PRE-DATES
WS5 — PRE-EXISTING, OBSERVATION, not a FAIL. WS5 fixed focus restoration
for the REFUSAL branch only (which is what the dispatch specifically asked
me to check and which passes); the SUCCESS branch's pre-existing gap is
untouched. Flagged for backlog — the fix pattern (refocus on
`htmx:afterRequest`) is now proven and adjacent in the same function.

**Required birth month.** `trace4_required_birthmonth.mjs`: new row via
"+ Add Person", typed a name, tabbed off the (still-blank, `required`) birth
month field → no `/whatif/settings` POST fires, `document.activeElement` is
the birth-month `<input>` with native `validationMessage: "Please fill out
this field."` — browser validity message shown, focus moves to it exactly
as specced. PASSES.

**Required glide fields — NOT stated in text.** `trace7_glide_required_marking.mjs`,
both fresh-reveal and post-error states: `glide-start-stock-pct`,
`glide-end-stock-pct`, `glide-transition-years` all have `required: false`,
no `aria-required`. `#glide-path-fields`' visible text on first reveal is
only "Start % End % Years Apply Glide Path" — no "(required)"/asterisk/
instructional text. The only place "all three required" is stated is
REACTIVELY, inside the role=alert error AFTER a failed submit
(rate-assumptions.html:425-448, diff lines ~872-896). This state — a user
seeing three blank, unmarked fields they must fill before Apply works — did
not exist before this task: pre-WS5 the checkbox auto-submitted on any tick
(`onchange="this.form.requestSubmit()"`) and the fields div only ever
rendered already-populated, when a glide path was already saved+enabled
(`{{if and .Settings.GlidePath .Settings.GlidePath.Enabled}}`) — confirmed
via `git show master` of this template. D6 introduces the reveal-then-fill
UI and, with it, a genuinely NEW state that is required-but-unmarked. The
same diff correctly added `required` to the birth-month input
(rate-assumptions.html:37) — showing the pattern is known and was applied
inconsistently within this very task.

FAIL — ACCESSIBILITY.md point 6 ("Required fields … are stated in text, not
implied by placeholder alone") / WCAG 2.2 SC 3.3.2 Labels or Instructions
(Level A, part of the AA baseline). File:
web/templates/components/whatif/rate-assumptions.html:425-448 (glide-path-
fields block, `start_stock_pct`/`end_stock_pct`/`transition_years` inputs).
Fix shape: add `required` (matching the birth-month field) and/or persistent
helper text ("All three fields are required to apply a glide path") visible
as soon as the fields are revealed, not only after a failed submit.

**Reflow 320/375px.** `trace5_reflow.mjs`/`trace6_overflow_source.mjs`: at
375px no horizontal overflow. At 320px, `document.documentElement.scrollWidth`
= 344 (24px overflow) — traced the actual overflowing element: an unrelated
"Add Expense" button (`class="px-3 py-1 bg-accent-strong text-white text-sm
rounded hover:bg-accent-strong"`, textContent "Add Expense") elsewhere on
the page, not any glide-path/person-row element WS5 touched (WS5.1.diff
never touches that markup). PRE-EXISTING — OBSERVATION.

**Motion.** No CSS transition or animation was added for
`#glide-path-fields`'s reveal (plain `classList.add/remove('hidden')`,
instant) — nothing here needs a `prefers-reduced-motion` guard. Point 15:
not applicable / no new motion introduced.

**Other structure.** No `<h1>`/landmark/heading changes in this diff; not
re-audited site-wide (out of this task's scope per the dispatch).

## FAILURES

1. ACCESSIBILITY.md point 6 / WCAG 2.2 SC 3.3.2 — glide-path Start %/End %/
   Years fields are required (server 400s if any is blank) but carry no
   `required`/`aria-required` and no persistent stated-in-text indication;
   the requirement is only discoverable reactively, after a failed submit.
   web/templates/components/whatif/rate-assumptions.html:425-448. New state
   introduced by this task's D6 reveal-then-apply redesign (unreachable
   before WS5).

## OBSERVATIONS (non-blocking, pre-existing or out of scope)

- Dark-mode color-contrast on `.mt-5 > summary` ("Adjust spending rules
  manually"), ratio 1.38 — byte-identical to master, unrelated section.
- Remove buttons' accessible name is bare "Remove" (no person name) in both
  the server template and the JS-generated row — byte-identical to master.
  Now more consequential given D7 makes Remove a real persisting/refusable
  action; recommend `aria-label="Remove {name}"`.
- Point 5's literal "linked via aria-describedby" is not implemented by any
  `/whatif` error (the sitewide `renderError`/base.js role=alert mechanism
  from WS4, unchanged here) — pre-existing, applies uniformly to WS5's two
  new error messages same as every other error on the page.
- On a SUCCESSFUL (non-refused) person removal, focus falls to `<body>` and
  is never restored — same root cause (`row.remove()`, no refocus) present
  in master's prior `removePersonRow`. WS5 fixed refocus for the refusal
  branch only; the success branch is an easy adjacent backlog fix.
- Glide checkbox has no `aria-expanded`/`aria-controls` — judged an
  acceptable equivalent given native checkbox state + adjacent-DOM reveal;
  cheap enhancement, not required.
- 320px horizontal overflow traced to an unrelated "Add Expense" button;
  WS5's own new content does not overflow at 320 or 375px.
